n Monday and fried chicken"},{"business_id":"8qCqw4c6XArdSQmWqdn0dw","review_id":"5H-3JOYDcqmrC6YavDJyzQ","date":"2007-10-20T08:21:29","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9297297596931458,"text_excerpt":"I haven't been there post-Katrina, but I'm not going to lie to you. Their Freret St location was sketch. I was a little nervous. Good thing they've got good, home-cooked, Southern comfort food. Go there on Monday's and get their red beans and rice with fried chicken. Damn DAMN good."},{"business_id":"8qCqw4c6XArdSQmWqdn0dw","review_id":"qizMr_R9RwqJmG2kKdPdLg","date":"2013-08-07T19:31:11","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9129770398139954,"text_excerpt":"$5 all you can eat red beans and rice and fried chicken. Free homemade sweet tea or lemonade with student ID! My absolute favorite soul food joint in the city. The family that runs it is so nice. On the Loyola Campus since Katrina hit."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
